    "title": "Popular anxiety prescription recalled nationwide",
    "text": "by: Matthew Euzarraga Posted: Apr 15, 2026 / 07:52 AM EDT Updated: Apr 15, 2026 / 10:49 AM EDT NEW YORK (PIX11) – A widely prescribed medication for treating anxiety and panic disorders is being recalled nationwide, according to the FDA. Xanax (alprazolam) pills are being voluntarily recalled by the American pharmaceutical company Viatris Inc. because the drug failed to meet dissolution specifications. Failure to meet dissolution specifications may indicate that the pill doesn’t deliver the correct dosage over time, that batch consistency is compromised, or that the absorption rate of the active ingredient into the bloodstream is affected, according to industry guidance. This may cause problems for patients who are on the popular drug, as alprazolam is one of the most commonly prescribed benzodiazepines in the United States, according to a study published by the National Institutes of Health. Recall information Product: Xanax XR, alprazolam, extended-release tablets, 3 mg, 60 Tablets bottles, Rx only, Distributed by: Viatris Specialty LLC, Morgantown, WV 06506, U.S.A, Made in Ireland, NDC 58151-506-91 Lot No. 8177156 Expiration date: 02/28/2027 The recall is classified as a class II recall, where use or exposure to a product may cause temporary or reversible adverse health effects, according to the FDA. For more information, click here. FOX 8 sister station PIX11 News reached out to Viatris Inc., but they were not immediately available to comment.",
